    "description": "- Feature-led a quarter-long, multi-engineer initiative to redesign a core permissions system for Jira Align, directly mitigating a $2.8M churn risk for a strategic customer and shipping a durable access-control model used by all customers.\n- Designed and implemented a scalable permissions architecture by modernizing fragile legacy checks into typed C# services, establishing the standard pattern for new access-control logic across the product.\n- Led end-to-end delivery across 60+ files and 12 areas of the stack, coordinating a core team and onboarding 5+ engineers as scope expanded; shipped with zero customer-reported bugs across multiple releases.\n- Pioneered the first asynchronous data-enrichment model for a large-scale planning and visualization product, unblocking enterprise adoption by decoupling enrichment workflows from core data loading.\n- Established a reusable, configuration-driven filtering framework adopted across multiple product surfaces, standardizing behavior and saving an estimated 500+ developer days.\n- Delivered measurable reliability and performance improvements, including resolving recurring production deadlocks and reducing P90 page load times by ~2.5 seconds through architectural and frontend optimizations.",
